{"id":"u-4be117c2-535d-4499-b27d-0acd6ef1dc02","src":"community","title":"Gym Prep - Strength & Mobility","author":"Travis M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/dTlB2Z-gym-prep-strength-and-mobility","desc":"4 Weeks | 5 Days per Week | 45 Minutes per Day\n\nGym Prep is a four-week program designed to prepare your body for regular strength training. Whether you're stepping into the gym for the first time or returning after a few months away, the goal is to gradually introduce exercise, improve range of motion, build strength, and prepare your muscles and joints for more demanding workouts.\n\nThe program consists of five 45-minute workouts per week: two upper-body days, two lower-body days, and one full-body day. Each session begins with five minutes of mobility exercises, followed by 35 minutes of strength training and five minutes of core work. All major muscle groups are trained at least twice weekly, with an emphasis on controlled movements, proper technique, and gradual progression. Workouts begin with lighter resistance and progress toward moderate resistance as your body adapts.\n\nBy the end of four weeks, the goal is to have improved strength, mobility, coordination, and overall exercise tolerance while establishing a consistent training routine. This foundation prepares you to transition into a more demanding program focused on muscle growth, strength, endurance, or general fitness. Gradually increasing your workload allows your body time to adapt and helps avoid unnecessary injury risks associated with progressing too quickly.","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-31T03:07:53.030Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper A","lower A","Upper B","Lower B","Day 5"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Arm Circle","sets":[{"sec":30}]},{"n":"Standing Shoulder Rolls 10 Each Way","sets":[{"sec":30}]},{"n":"Thoracic Spine Rotations","sets":[{"sec":6